## Three.js, live: the neon city to fly and walk through in a browser.
## The city is the same arrays as the ray-traced film (blender's
## demos/NeonCity.xtl), written as the same calls (Cycles.xtl); here
## they go to a player written with Three.js. This writes a directory
## to serve, work/city: the page, the player, Three.js and the calls.
## Run: just ext three city   (then just ext three serve city, and open
## http://127.0.0.1:8470/)
## Command: just ext three city && just ext three serve city
## Page: three/live/ fly and walk through it, live

"th:" u_se< "Three"
"nc:" u_se< "NeonCity"

scene := (nc:seed, 1280, 720, 30, 24, "GPU") nc:c_ity 0
"the calls of the scene, and the files written to work/city:"
th:s_how! scene
"work/city" th:p_age! scene
